# The operator's real configuration. It carries SYMONEURAL_MINER_TOKEN — the shared secret that
# gates start/stop of a process which takes the GPU — and a wallet address. The tracked
# file is miner.env.example, which is inert by design.
miner.env

# The root .gitignore has `*.log`, which is right for run/ and wrong for exactly one file
# here: testdata/ holds captured miner output that `test_miner.py` asserts against
# byte-for-byte. Without this negation the fixture is never committed and the suite fails on
# a fresh checkout with "missing capture" -- while passing on the machine that wrote it,
# which is the worst way for a test to be broken. A deeper .gitignore can re-include a file
# a shallower one excluded, as long as no parent directory is itself excluded; `*.log`
# excludes files, so this works.
!testdata/*.log
